WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.836
Your first course with EP Courses.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:07.987
From an empty PageMotor site to a course a student can enrol in and finish.

00:00:07.987 --> 00:00:10.392
You create two pages, and only two.

00:00:11.792 --> 00:00:15.659
Start with the one idea that makes everything else obvious.

00:00:15.659 --> 00:00:17.101
Courses are not pages.

00:00:17.101 --> 00:00:22.345
They live in a catalogue inside the plugin, the way products live inside a shop.

00:00:22.345 --> 00:00:27.326
The viewer page you make is a television set, and every course is a channel.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:31.784
One page, and the link someone clicks decides which course it shows.

00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:35.848
So you never make a page per course, and never one per lesson.

00:00:37.248 --> 00:00:38.221
So, two pages.

00:00:38.221 --> 00:00:43.366
One with the slug course-viewer, holding the shortcode [ep-course-viewer].

00:00:43.366 --> 00:00:51.780
That is the single page where every course is watched, and every Enrol and Continue button the plugin draws points at it.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:58.872
The other has the slug courses and holds [ep-courses], which renders every published course as a card.

00:00:58.872 --> 00:01:02.279
The plugin writes every link between them itself.

00:01:03.679 --> 00:01:07.440
Before you feed it your own material, drive the sample.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:15.101
EP Courses planted a course called Getting Started the first time it ran, and it exists for exactly this moment.

00:01:15.101 --> 00:01:20.025
Enrol, click through all three lessons, and watch the progress bar fill.

00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:21.735
Then leave and come back:

00:01:21.735 --> 00:01:27.549
the button now reads Continue Learning, and drops you at your next unfinished lesson.

00:01:28.949 --> 00:01:33.214
Now your own course. Two fields decide more than all the rest.

00:01:33.214 --> 00:01:44.704
Category is free text you invent, lowercase with hyphens, and it must be spelt identically on every course in that area, because the filtering later is an exact match.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:54.955
Access is the free-versus-paid switch, and you keep everything Free while you build, because a Premium course reads Coming Soon and nobody can enrol.

00:01:56.355 --> 00:02:00.647
Lessons are plain HTML, and four tags cover an entire course:

00:02:00.647 --> 00:02:03.532
a paragraph, a heading, a list, and bold.

00:02:03.532 --> 00:02:06.628
Students only ever see the formatted result.

00:02:06.628 --> 00:02:14.931
Writing the material is the work, wrapping it in tags is not, so hand your notes to Claude and ask it to do that part.

00:02:16.331 --> 00:02:18.656
Video is just a type and a URL:

00:02:18.656 --> 00:02:23.531
YouTube, Vimeo, or an MP4 anywhere, including your own S3 bucket.

00:02:23.531 --> 00:02:28.856
But if you are selling the course, protect the file, not just the page.

00:02:28.856 --> 00:02:37.181
Enrolment gates the lesson, while the video link behind it can be copied, shared, and it keeps working forever.

00:02:37.181 --> 00:02:45.356
EP Media Storage serves each one through a link that expires, so a copied one is dead by the time it travels.

00:02:46.756 --> 00:02:53.459
Once your site has areas, give each one its own list page with a filtered copy of the same shortcode.

00:02:53.459 --> 00:02:58.237
One category per page, and the spelling has to match the course exactly.

00:02:58.237 --> 00:03:02.550
One typing note: the quote marks must be the plain straight kind.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:10.115
Word processors curl them into something the shortcode cannot read, and then it renders as plain text on the page.

00:03:11.515 --> 00:03:21.122
Before real students arrive, remember that watching a lesson needs a login even on a free course, because progress is tracked per student.

00:03:21.122 --> 00:03:27.038
That is EP Membership's department, and the register page has to exist by launch day.

00:03:27.038 --> 00:03:30.101
Two of its switches deserve a warning label.

00:03:30.101 --> 00:03:44.163
Welcome Email and Require Email Verification both send through your site's own email plumbing, so leave them off until that is actually working, or new members sit waiting for a link that never arrives.

00:03:45.563 --> 00:03:51.228
The guide has every field, the troubleshooting for each thing that goes wrong, and where to go next.
